  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 242 PM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nInto the end of the work week, the ridge over the southeastern CONUS \nflattens out somewhat, but still generally keeps its influence over \nIowa, which will allow for the continuation of rather uncomfortable \nconditions with the heat and humidity. Forecast highs in mid 90s and \nheat indices around 100-105 degrees over much of southern Iowa are \nexpected, which could lead to an extension in current heat \nheadlines into Friday if forecast trends continue to lean that \nway, so stay tuned for updates. Additional shortwaves traveling \nthrough the western periphery of this ridge will continue to \nbring continued periods of showers and thunderstorms, \nparticularly during the overnight and morning Thursday and \nFriday. Location of the associated boundary(s) and the influence\nof the cap overhead are still generally uncertain in this \nrange, and even more so through the weekend considering how \nearlier activity in the week plays out, so will need to monitor \ntrends over the coming days. For now, have left at least low PoP\nmentions over portions of the forecast area through the period \ngiven this overall potential.",
